  "language_probability": 1,
  "text": "Touch this spot. How does the glass know where your finger landed? Beneath it, transparent electrodes cross in rows and columns. Each crossing holds a tiny electric field. Watch the center crossing. Your finger draws a little charge so this field changes. The other crossings stay nearly unchanged. The controller finds the changed row and column. Their intersection becomes the touch position. A normal glove stops this effect. Conductive thread lets it through, so the crossing responds again. That is how glass turns a changed electric field into a touch location.",
